    ("faust-part-one-goethe", "Faust, Part One", "Johann Wolfgang von Goethe", "1749 – 1832", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "Poetry & Drama", 1808, "Romanticism", "Advanced", "📜", 14591, 45000,
     "Goethe's supreme poetic drama of Faust's pact with Mephistopheles in pursuit of ultimate knowledge, beauty, and experience.", ["The Faustian Striving", "The Pact with Mephistopheles", "Knowledge and Transgression", "Redemption through Spirit"], "Prologue in Heaven", "The Sun-orb sings, in ancient tourney, with brother-spheres a rival song; and, with commanded march, his journey moves with thunder-sound along.", "Faust: Eine Tragödie", "de"),
    ("the-sorrows-of-young-werther-goethe", "The Sorrows of Young Werther", "Johann Wolfgang von Goethe", "1749 – 1832", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "World Literature", 1774, "Sturm und Drang", "Intermediate", "💌", 2527, 44000,
     "The epoch-making epistolary novel of passionate idealism, youthful sensibility, and profound romantic longing.", ["Sturm und Drang Sensibility", "Nature and the Heart", "Unrequited Devotion", "Romantic Melancholy"], "May 4th: Joy in Nature", "How happy I am that I am gone! My dear friend, what a thing is the heart of man! To leave you, whom I love so much, from whom I was inseparable, and yet to feel happy!", "Die Leiden des jungen Werthers", "de"),
    ("metamorphosis-kafka", "The Metamorphosis", "Franz Kafka", "1883 – 1924", "Austria", "Europe", "German & English", "Fiction & Fantasy", 1915, "Modernism", "Intermediate", "🪲", 5200, 22000,
     "Gregor Samsa awakens to discover he has transformed into an insect, exploring alienation, family duty, and modern existence.", ["Alienation and Identity", "Family Burden and Guilt", "Absurdist Reality", "The Human Condition"], "The Awakening", "One morning, when Gregor Samsa woke from troubled dreams, he found himself transformed in his bed into a horrible vermin.", "Die Verwandlung", "de"),
    ("the-trial-kafka", "The Trial", "Franz Kafka", "1883 – 1924", "Austria", "Europe", "German & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", 1925, "Modernism", "Advanced", "⚖️", 7849, 82000,
     "Josef K. is arrested by an enigmatic and invisible court system, creating the definitive modern allegory of bureaucratic dread.", ["Bureaucratic Absurdity", "Inscrutable Justice", "Guilt without Crime", "Existential Inquiry"], "The Arrest", "Someone must have slandered Josef K., for one morning, without having done anything truly wrong, he was arrested.", "Der Process", "de"),
    ("thus-spoke-zarathustra-nietzsche", "Thus Spoke Zarathustra", "Friedrich Nietzsche", "1844 – 1900", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", 1883, "19th Century", "Advanced", "⛰️", 1998, 110000,
     "Nietzsche's poetic philosophical masterpiece on human potential, self-overcoming, eternal recurrence, and spiritual renewal.", ["Self-Overcoming", "The Will to Create", "Eternal Recurrence", "The Solitude of the Mountain"], "Zarathustra's Prologue", "When Zarathustra was thirty years old, he left his home and the lake of his home, and went into the mountains. There he enjoyed his spirit and his solitude.", "Also sprach Zarathustra", "de"),
    ("beyond-good-and-evil-nietzsche", "Beyond Good and Evil", "Friedrich Nietzsche", "1844 – 1900", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", 1886, "19th Century", "Advanced", "⚡", 4363, 76000,
     "A provocative critique of dogmatic philosophy and moral presuppositions, advocating for intellectual honesty and courageous thinking.", ["Critique of Dogmatism", "The Free Spirit", "Perspectivism in Knowledge", "Courageous Inquiry"], "On the Prejudices of Philosophers", "The Will to Truth, which is to tempt us to many a hazardous enterprise, the famous Truthfulness of which all philosophers have hitherto spoken with respect, what questions has this Will to Truth not laid before us!", "Jenseits von Gut und Böse", "de"),
    ("critique-of-pure-reason-kant", "Critique of Pure Reason", "Immanuel Kant", "1724 – 1804", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "Mathematics & Logic", 1781, "Enlightenment", "Advanced", "🧠", 4280, 225000,
     "The watershed revolution in epistemology, synthesizing rationalism and empiricism through a priori synthetic judgments.", ["Synthetic A Priori Judgments", "Space and Time as Intuitions", "The Limits of Pure Reason", "Categories of the Understanding"], "Introduction to Pure Reason", "There can be no doubt that all our knowledge begins with experience. For how should our faculty of knowledge be awakened into action did not objects affecting our senses stir it?", "Kritik der reinen Vernunft", "de"),
    ("perpetual-peace-kant", "Perpetual Peace: A Philosophical Sketch", "Immanuel Kant", "1724 – 1804", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "History & Civilizations", 1795, "Enlightenment", "Advanced", "🕊️", 50922, 28000,
     "Kant's prophetic blueprint for a federation of constitutional republics, universal hospitality, and lasting international peace.", ["Federation of Free States", "Universal Hospitality", "Republican Constitution", "Philosophical Conditions of Peace"], "Preliminary Articles", "'Perpetual Peace'—A Dutch innkeeper once put this satirical inscription on his sign, with a painting of a graveyard. Does this hold for men in general, or for rulers in particular?", "Zum ewigen Frieden", "de"),
    ("grimms-fairy-tales", "Grimm's Fairy Tales", "Jacob & Wilhelm Grimm", "1785 – 1863", "Germany", "Europe", "German & English", "Children's Literature", 1812, "Romanticism", "Beginner", "🏰", 2591, 140000,
     "The foundational world treasury of German folk literature, featuring Cinderella, Hansel and Gretel, Rapunzel, and Rumpelstiltskin.", ["Folk Wisdom and Morals", "Wonder and Transformation", "Courage and Resourcefulness", "The German Oral Tradition"], "The Frog King", "In olden times when wishing still helped one, there lived a king whose daughters were all beautiful; and the youngest was so beautiful that the sun itself, which has seen so much, was astonished whenever it shone in her face.", "Kinder- und Hausmärchen", "de"),

    # --- JAPAN ---
    ("the-tale-of-genji-shikibu", "The Tale of Genji (Selected Chapters)", "Murasaki Shikibu", "c. 973 – c. 1014", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "International Classics", 1008, "Heian Era", "Advanced", "🌸", 40150, 180000,
     "Widely celebrated as the world's first novel, a luminous chronicle of court life, aesthetic refinement, and mono no aware.", ["Mono no Aware (Pathos of Things)", "Heian Court Aesthetics", "Waka Poetic Exchange", "Transience of Human Glory"], "The Paulownia Pavilion (Kiritsubo)", "In a certain reign there was a lady who, though she was not of very high rank was favoured far beyond all the rest; so that the great ladies in the palace were very jealous.", "源氏物語", "ja"),
    ("the-pillow-book-shonagon", "The Pillow Book (Makura no Sōshi)", "Sei Shōnagon", "c. 966 – c. 1025", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "World Literature", 1002, "Heian Era", "Intermediate", "🪶", 52101, 85000,
     "Witty, observant, and intimate court diary entries celebrating nature, seasonal beauty, courtly elegance, and personal hates.", ["Seasonal Observations", "Aesthetic Judgments (Okashi)", "Heian Courtiers", "Poetic Lists and Musings"], "In Spring the Dawn", "In spring it is the dawn that is most delightful. As the light creeps over the hills, their outlines are dyed a faint red and wisps of purplish cloud trail over them.", "枕草子", "ja"),
    ("the-narrow-road-to-the-deep-north-basho", "The Narrow Road to the Deep North (Oku no Hosomichi)", "Matsuo Bashō", "1644 – 1694", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "Poetry & Drama", 1694, "Edo Period", "Intermediate", "🍃", 52102, 24000,
     "The pinnacle of haibun travel literature, combining spare evocative prose and sublime haiku across northern Japan.", ["The Journey as Life", "Haiku and Wabi-Sabi", "Solitary Wandering", "Communion with Nature"], "Departure for the North", "The moon and sun are eternal travelers. Even the years that come and go are on a journey of their own. Those who float away their lives on boats, or meet their old age leading a horse by the bit, spend every day traveling, and travel is their home.", "奥の細道", "ja"),
    ("night-on-the-galactic-railroad-miyazawa", "Night on the Galactic Railroad (Ginga Tetsudō no Yoru)", "Kenji Miyazawa", "1896 – 1933", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "Children's Literature", 1927, "Early 20th Century", "Beginner", "🌌", 52103, 38000,
     "Giovanni and Campanella board a magical train traversing the luminous Milky Way, exploring friendship, self-sacrifice, and true happiness.", ["Cosmic Wonder and Compassion", "Selfless Happiness for All", "The Stellar Sea", "Friendship and Loss"], "The Centaurus Festival", "'Now then, what is that river of milky white that stretches across the sky?' the teacher asked, pointing to a large constellation chart hanging before the blackboard.", "銀河鉄道の夜", "ja"),
    ("the-restaurant-of-many-orders-miyazawa", "The Restaurant of Many Orders (Chūmon no Ōi Ryōriten)", "Kenji Miyazawa", "1896 – 1933", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "Children's Literature", 1924, "Early 20th Century", "Beginner", "🚪", 52104, 18000,
     "Two proud hunters get lost in a deep mountain forest and find a strange Western restaurant that makes increasingly curious demands.", ["Respect for Nature and Animals", "Humility vs Greed", "Forest Wonder and Satire", "Clever Twist of Expectations"], "The Mountain Forest", "Two young gentlemen, dressed in immaculate British hunting suits and carrying gleaming modern rifles, were tramping through the deep woods of the northern mountains.", "注文の多い料理店", "ja"),
    ("kokoro-natsume-soseki", "Kokoro", "Natsume Sōseki", "1867 – 1916", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "International Classics", 1914, "Early 20th Century", "Advanced", "❤️", 52105, 88000,
     "A youth's friendship with the enigmatic 'Sensei' and Sensei's final testament on love, guilt, betrayal, and Meiji spiritual change.", ["The Mystery of the Human Heart", "Guilt and Honor", "Transition from Meiji to Modernity", "Generational Alienation"], "Sensei and I", "I always called him 'Sensei.' I shall therefore refer to him simply as 'Sensei,' and not by his real name. It is not because I wish to be secretive, but because it feels more natural to me.", "こゝろ", "ja"),
    ("i-am-a-cat-natsume-soseki", "I Am a Cat (Wagahai wa Neko de Aru)", "Natsume Sōseki", "1867 – 1916", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "World Literature", 1905, "Early 20th Century", "Intermediate", "🐾", 52106, 175000,
     "A nameless philosophic feline comments with devastating wit on the pretentious intellectual discussions of his human owner's circle.", ["Satirical View of Human Folly", "Feline Philosophy", "Meiji Intellectual Vanity", "Humorous Observation"], "The Nameless Cat", "I am a cat. As yet I have no name. I've no idea where I was born. All I remember is that I was miaowing in a dampish dark place when for the first time I saw a human being.", "吾輩は猫である", "ja"),
    ("rashomon-akutagawa", "Rashōmon and In a Grove", "Ryūnosuke Akutagawa", "1892 – 1927", "Japan", "Asia", "Japanese & English", "Mystery & Adventure", 1915, "Early 20th Century", "Intermediate", "⛩️", 52107, 32000,
     "Akutagawa's landmark psychological investigations into subjective perception, moral survival, and multiple contradictory testimonies.", ["Subjective Truth and Reality", "Moral Survival in Collapse", "Multiple Perspectives", "Heian Atmosphere"], "Beneath the Gate", "It was a chilly evening. A servant of a samurai was waiting under the Rashōmon for the rain to cease. In the wide space beneath the great gate, there was no one else.", "羅生門", "ja"),

    # --- CHINA ---
    ("the-art-of-war-sun-tzu", "The Art of War", "Sun Tzu", "c. 544 – c. 496 BCE", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", -500, "Ancient Era", "Intermediate", "⚔️", 132, 22000,
     "The definitive ancient manual of strategic wisdom, emphasizing victory without conflict, tactical flexibility, and self-knowledge.", ["Strategic Intelligence", "Winning without Battle", "Self-Knowledge and Knowing the Opponent", "Flexibility and Timing"], "Laying Plans", "Sun Tzu said: The art of war is of vital importance to the State. It is a matter of life and death, a road either to safety or to ruin. Hence it is a subject of inquiry which can on no account be neglected.", "孫子兵法", "zh"),
    ("the-analects-confucius", "The Analects of Confucius (Lunyu)", "Confucius", "551 – 479 BCE", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", -475, "Ancient Era", "Intermediate", "📜", 4094, 48000,
     "The foundational collection of sayings and dialogues on benevolence (Ren), filial piety (Xiao), ritual propriety (Li), and righteous leadership.", ["Benevolence (Ren)", "Filial Piety (Xiao)", "Moral Exemplar (Junzi)", "Harmony through Learning"], "On Learning and Friendship", "The Master said: 'Is it not pleasant to learn with a constant perseverance and application? Is it not delightful to have friends coming from distant quarters?'", "論語", "zh"),
    ("dao-de-jing-laozi", "Dao De Jing (Tao Te Ching)", "Laozi", "c. 6th Century BCE", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", -500, "Ancient Era", "Intermediate", "☯️", 216, 16000,
     "The poetic and timeless scripture of Daoism, illuminating the Way (Dao), effortless action (Wu-wei), simplicity, and softness overcoming strength.", ["The Unnameable Way", "Effortless Action (Wu Wei)", "Water as Virtue", "Simplicity and Humility"], "The Dao that can be told", "The Dao that can be trodden is not the enduring and unchanging Dao. The name that can be named is not the enduring and unchanging name.", "道德經", "zh"),
    ("the-zhuangzi-inner-chapters", "The Zhuangzi (Inner Chapters)", "Zhuangzi", "c. 369 – c. 286 BCE", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "Philosophy & Psychology", -300, "Ancient Era", "Advanced", "🦋", 27076, 52000,
     "Imaginative parables, the Butterfly Dream, the useless tree, and spontaneous harmony with the transformations of Nature.", ["The Butterfly Dream", "Relativity of Truth and Value", "Carefree Wandering (Xiaoyao)", "The Fasting of the Heart"], "Carefree Wandering", "In the Northern Ocean there is a fish called the Kun, whose size is many thousand li across. It transforms into a bird called the Peng, whose back is like Mount Tai and wings like clouds hanging from heaven.", "莊子", "zh"),
    ("records-of-the-grand-historian-sima-qian", "Records of the Grand Historian (Shiji: Selected Biographies)", "Sima Qian", "c. 145 – c. 86 BCE", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "History & Civilizations", -94, "Han Dynasty", "Advanced", "🏯", 52201, 140000,
     "The monumental masterpiece of Chinese historiography detailing dynasties, generals, assassins, and philosophers with dramatic psychological depth.", ["Biographical Truth and History", "Moral Duty and Dignity", "The Fall and Rise of States", "Courage in Adversity"], "Preface and First Dynasties", "Sima Qian, the Grand Astrologer, said: My father Sima Tan was an officer of the Han court, and when he lay dying, he took my hand and wept, asking that I continue the records of the empire.", "史記", "zh"),
    ("dream-of-the-red-chamber-cao-xueqin", "Dream of the Red Chamber (Story of the Stone)", "Cao Xueqin", "c. 1715 – 1763", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "International Classics", 1791, "Qing Dynasty", "Advanced", "💎", 24264, 450000,
     "The crowning jewel of classical Chinese vernacular literature detailing the splendor and spiritual awakening of the Jia family.", ["Illusion and Spiritual Awakening", "The Splendor of the Grand View Garden", "Love between Baoyu and Daiyu", "Transience of Dynastic Glory"], "The Stone and the Monk", "Long ago, when the goddess Nüwa was repairing the heavens, she melted down stones to patch the blue sky. One stone was left unused at the foot of the Baseless Mountain.", "紅樓夢", "zh"),
    ("romance-of-the-three-kingdoms-luo-guanzhong", "Romance of the Three Kingdoms (Sanguo Yanyi)", "Luo Guanzhong", "c. 1330 – 1400", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "History & Civilizations", 1522, "Ming Dynasty", "Advanced", "🐎", 52202, 380000,
     "The epic chronicle of brotherhood, political strategy, and heroic battles dividing the Han dynasty into Shu, Wei, and Wu.", ["Brotherhood at the Peach Garden", "Strategic Genius of Zhuge Liang", "Loyalty, Honor, and Betrayal", "The Flow of World Empires"], "The Oath of the Peach Garden", "The empire, long divided, must unite; long united, must divide. Thus it has ever been. In the closing years of the Eastern Han dynasty, the Yellow Turbans raised rebellion.", "三國演義", "zh"),
    ("journey-to-the-west-wu-chengen", "Journey to the West (The Monkey King)", "Wu Cheng'en", "c. 1500 – 1582", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "Fiction & Fantasy", 1592, "Ming Dynasty", "Intermediate", "🐒", 52203, 310000,
     "The immortal mythological quest of Sun Wukong, Tang Monk, Pigsy, and Sandy traveling to India to retrieve Buddhist scriptures.", ["Sun Wukong's Rebellion in Heaven", "The Journey to the Western Pure Land", "Disciplining the Mind-Monkey", "Humor and Buddhist Parable"], "Birth of the Stone Monkey", "Beyond the sea there lay the country of Aolai. Near the ocean was the Mountain of Flowers and Fruit. On the peak stood a magic stone, which had been nourished by Heaven and Earth since the creation.", "西遊記", "zh"),
    ("the-true-story-of-ah-q-lu-xun", "The True Story of Ah Q and Call to Arms", "Lu Xun", "1881 – 1936", "China", "Asia", "Chinese & English", "World Literature", 1921, "Early 20th Century", "Intermediate", "🏮", 25482, 54000,
     "Lu Xun's foundational modernist masterpiece satirizing spiritual victories, complacency, and awakening Chinese national consciousness.", ["Spiritual Victory Method", "Satire on Complacency", "Social Awakening and Revolution", "Realism and Compassion"], "Introduction to Ah Q", "For several years now I have been meaning to write the true story of Ah Q. But while wanting to write it, I was in two minds about doing so.", "阿Q正傳", "zh"),

